===============================================================================
                    NOT FINANCIAL ADVICE - READ THIS
===============================================================================

This software is a RESEARCH AND MEASUREMENT tool. It exists to test whether
trading strategies work, and the honest answer it keeps returning is that they
do not.

NOTHING IN THIS REPOSITORY HAS PASSED ITS OWN LIVE-READINESS GATES.

At the time of publication, measured on this project's own data:

  - Six signal families were tested. All six were net-negative after costs.
  - Of 87 (asset x style) cells, ZERO cleared all four validation gates.
  - Of 155,017 backtested candidates, the best deflated Sharpe was 0.702,
    below the 0.95 bar, meaning its edge is not clearly distinguishable
    from the luck of having searched 155,017 candidates.
  - Published opening-range-breakout rules measured 0 of 24 profitable years.

The reports in this repository document those results in full, including the
cases where a promising result was retracted after further testing.

Trading involves substantial risk of loss, including total loss of capital.
Past performance -- backtested or live -- does not indicate future results.
A backtest is not a promise; it is a measurement of the past under assumptions
that are stated in the code and are certainly incomplete.

The authors and contributors are not investment advisers, accept no liability
for any decision taken using this software, and strongly recommend that you do
not risk money you cannot afford to lose.

Independently verify every number before acting on it. The tooling here is
built to make that verification possible; please use it for that.
